{
 "id": "2026-10-25-aliasing-nyquist",
 "topic": "aliasing: why sampling must be faster than twice the frequency (Nyquist)",
 "subject": "engineering",
 "hook_type": "myth bust",
 "caption": "Sample a 9 Hz wave 10 times a second and the dots trace a perfectly smooth 1 Hz wave: the data can't tell them apart. That's aliasing. To pin down a frequency f you need more than 2f samples per second, which is why audio CDs sample at 44.1 kHz.\n\nSave this for your signals and systems course.\n\n#engineering #signalprocessing #nyquist #aliasing #electricalengineering #math #stem #dsp #audio",
 "cover_at": 1.0,
 "hook": "Myth: sample a signal faster than it wiggles, and you've captured it.",
 "beats": [
  {
   "text": "Here's a sine wave oscillating 9 times per second, over one second.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "axes",
     "name": "ax",
     "x": [
      0,
      1.05,
      0.25
     ],
     "y": [
      -1.3,
      1.3,
      1
     ],
     "size": [
      7.6,
      4.2
     ],
     "at": [
      0,
      2.6
     ],
     "labels": [
      "t",
      "y"
     ]
    },
    {
     "make": "graph",
     "name": "g9",
     "on": "ax",
     "fn": "sin(2*pi*9*x)",
     "x": [
      0,
      1
     ],
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "l9",
     "tex": [
      "f",
      "=",
      "9\\text{ Hz}"
     ],
     "size": 72,
     "at": [
      0,
      5.6
     ],
     "colors": {
      "2": "blue"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Now measure it only 10 times per second. That's faster than it oscillates, so it should be enough. Right?",
   "do": [
    {
     "together": [
      {
       "make": "dot",
       "name": "d0",
       "on": "ax",
       "at": [
        0.0,
        0.0
       ],
       "color": "yellow"
      },
      {
       "make": "dot",
       "name": "d1",
       "on": "ax",
       "at": [
        0.1,
        -0.5878
       ],
       "color": "yellow"
      },
      {
       "make": "dot",
       "name": "d2",
       "on": "ax",
       "at": [
        0.2,
        -0.9511
       ],
       "color": "yellow"
      },
      {
       "make": "dot",
       "name": "d3",
       "on": "ax",
       "at": [
        0.3,
        -0.9511
       ],
       "color": "yellow"
      },
      {
       "make": "dot",
       "name": "d4",
       "on": "ax",
       "at": [
        0.4,
        -0.5878
       ],
       "color": "yellow"
      },
      {
       "make": "dot",
       "name": "d5",
       "on": "ax",
       "at": [
        0.5,
        0.0
       ],
       "color": "yellow"
      },
      {
       "make": "dot",
       "name": "d6",
       "on": "ax",
       "at": [
        0.6,
        0.5878
       ],
       "color": "yellow"
      },
      {
       "make": "dot",
       "name": "d7",
       "on": "ax",
       "at": [
        0.7,
        0.9511
       ],
       "color": "yellow"
      },
      {
       "make": "dot",
       "name": "d8",
       "on": "ax",
       "at": [
        0.8,
        0.9511
       ],
       "color": "yellow"
      },
      {
       "make": "dot",
       "name": "d9",
       "on": "ax",
       "at": [
        0.9,
        0.5878
       ],
       "color": "yellow"
      },
      {
       "make": "dot",
       "name": "d10",
       "on": "ax",
       "at": [
        1.0,
        -0.0
       ],
       "color": "yellow"
      }
     ],
     "lag": 0.12
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "fs",
     "tex": [
      "f_s",
      "=",
      "10\\text{ Hz}"
     ],
     "size": 72,
     "at": [
      0,
      -0.5
     ],
     "colors": {
      "2": "yellow"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Keep only the samples, and forget the wave you started with.",
   "do": [
    {
     "hide": "g9",
     "time": 0.8
    },
    {
     "hide": "l9",
     "time": 0.3
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Join the dots, and a completely different wave appears: one slow oscillation per second.",
   "do": [
    {
     "sfx": "riser"
    },
    {
     "make": "graph",
     "name": "g1",
     "on": "ax",
     "fn": "-sin(2*pi*x)",
     "x": [
      0,
      1
     ],
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "sfx": "thud"
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "al",
     "tex": [
      "|\\,9 - 10\\,|",
      "=",
      "1\\text{ Hz}"
     ],
     "size": 80,
     "next_to": "fs",
     "buff": 0.4,
     "colors": {
      "2": "red"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Both waves pass through every sample exactly. From the data alone, you can't tell them apart.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "graph",
     "name": "g9b",
     "on": "ax",
     "fn": "sin(2*pi*9*x)",
     "x": [
      0,
      1
     ],
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "indicate": [
      "d0",
      "d1",
      "d2",
      "d3",
      "d4",
      "d5",
      "d6",
      "d7",
      "d8",
      "d9",
      "d10"
     ],
     "color": "yellow"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "do": [
    {
     "clear": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "That's aliasing. To pin down a frequency $f$, you need more than two samples per cycle.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "ny",
     "tex": [
      "f_s",
      ">",
      "2f"
     ],
     "size": 140,
     "at": [
      0,
      3.0
     ],
     "colors": {
      "0": "yellow",
      "2": "blue"
     }
    },
    {
     "sfx": "ding"
    },
    {
     "make": "box",
     "name": "bx",
     "around": "ny"
    },
    {
     "make": "text",
     "name": "nyl",
     "text": "the Nyquist rate",
     "size": 56,
     "color": "dim",
     "next_to": "ny",
     "buff": 0.6
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "For our 9 Hz wave, that means more than 18 samples per second, not 10.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "n18",
     "tex": [
      "f_s",
      ">",
      "18\\text{ Hz}"
     ],
     "size": 90,
     "at": [
      0,
      -0.2
     ],
     "colors": {
      "0": "yellow",
      "2": "green"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "It's why CDs sample at 44.1 kHz, just over twice the 20 kHz limit of human hearing.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "cd",
     "tex": [
      "44.1\\text{ kHz}",
      ">",
      "2 \\times 20\\text{ kHz}"
     ],
     "size": 80,
     "next_to": "n18",
     "buff": 0.6,
     "colors": {
      "0": "green"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "And why wheels in films seem to spin backwards: the camera samples too slowly.",
   "do": [
    {
     "indicate": "ny",
     "color": "yellow"
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "outro": "Follow for more ideas like this.",
